		{"id":"efb94fa0e3df213a","type":"text","text":"# Bucketing Dataframe\n\n## Bucketing versus partitioning\n\n| Partitioning | Bucketing |\n|---|---|\n| Creates directories for column values | Creates a fixed number of hash groups |\n| Good for low-cardinality columns | Good for high-cardinality columns |\n| Examples: `country`, `year`, `month` | Examples: `customer_id`, `account_id` |\n| Supports partition pruning | Mainly helps joins and aggregations |\n| Number of partitions depends on values | Number of buckets is fixed |","x":635,"y":-1557,"width":495,"height":480},
